# Resolve packages from the public npm registry.
#
# Why this file exists: this machine's user-level ~/.npmrc points npm at a
# private corporate Artifactory mirror. That works locally because the developer
# is authenticated to it, but it writes that host into every `resolved` URL in
# package-lock.json — and any build runner outside the corporate network (Vercel,
# GitHub Actions, a colleague's laptop) then fails to install, because it cannot
# reach or authenticate to that host.
#
# Pinning the public registry here keeps the lockfile portable and keeps this
# personal project off internal infrastructure.
#
# If your network blocks registry.npmjs.org, delete this file to fall back to
# your user-level registry — but regenerate the lockfile with
#   npm install --package-lock-only --registry=https://registry.npmjs.org
# before pushing, or deployments will break again.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
